  "query_preview": "..\nSuper Typhoon Bavi will continue to move to the west-northwest and\naway from the Marianas this evening. Trailing rain bands behind the\ntyphoon will continue to bring periods of numerous to widespread \nshowers and isolated to scattered thunderstorms in the storm's wake.\nFlooding impacts will be further exacerbated or new instances of \nflooding will be possible with additional heavy rainfall. Outer bands\nfrom Bavi will continue to impact the islands into Tuesday with \nperiods of heavy showers and isolated thunderstorms continuing \nthrough the day. Slightly drier weather will begin on Wednesday with \nshower chances dropping to lower-end scattered with thunderstorm \nchances continuing to decrease through Thursday. Shower coverage is \nexpected to drop to isolated for all islands by Friday. Tropical \nstorm force winds (sustained up to 58 mph) will continue for all \nislands through early Tuesday morning with conditions gradually \nimproving through Tuesday, though quite breezy conditions will \nlikely continue through much of the day.",
